---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import IntakeForm from '../islands/IntakeForm.svelte';
import { href } from '../lib/href';
const relay = process.env.PUBLIC_NLD_RELAY ?? 'https://landback-nld-relay.vercel.app';
---

<Page
  title="Claim or correct a page"
  lede="Every nation’s page in this atlas can be claimed by that nation: reviewed, corrected, told in its own words, or taken down."
>
  <p>
    The pages were built from federal records, court decisions, and research. None of it speaks for
    any nation, and no nation has reviewed it yet. If a page concerns your nation, you decide what
    happens to it.
  </p>
  <h2>What claiming a page means</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>We mark the page as under your nation’s review and hold any changes you ask for.</li>
    <li>
      Your nation can add its own account, in its own words and its own names, credited to the
      office you choose.
    </li>
    <li>You choose the license for anything you contribute. It never defaults to ours.</li>
    <li>Review is not endorsement: a reviewed page says only that your nation reviewed it.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Taking content down</h2>
  <p>
    A removal request is honored first and discussed second. The page and every link to it are
    hidden at the next build. If you want, the address shows a short note that the content was
    withdrawn at your nation’s request; if you prefer, it shows nothing.
  </p>
  <h2>Write to us</h2>
  <IntakeForm client:load {relay} />
  <p class="small muted">
    Not writing for a nation? To report an error, use the{' '}
    <a href={href('/corrections/')}>corrections page</a>. More about how review works:{' '}
    <a href={href('/for-tribal-reviewers/')}>for tribal reviewers</a>.
  </p>
</Page>
